1
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,000
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,000
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,000
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,933
[The Salvation Army Red Kettle]

5
00:00:49,472 --> 00:00:51,680
Merry Christmas!

6
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:00,928
Merry Christmas!

7
00:01:14,336 --> 00:01:16,616
What is it?

8
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,900
Ji Ah, I got you a present.

9
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:52,933
Wow! A teddy bear!

10
00:01:52,933 --> 00:01:55,567
Thank you so much, Daddy!

11
00:02:31,933 --> 00:02:36,000
It's been seven years
since I last saw your face.

12
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,167
I've missed you so much all that time.

13
00:02:47,008 --> 00:02:53,267
More than anything,
I'm sorry for leaving you all alone.

14
00:02:56,467 --> 00:02:58,967
I've blamed myself every single day.

15
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:02,433
That day...

16
00:03:04,433 --> 00:03:07,133
I shouldn't have done that that day.

17
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:21,067
I think something got into it.
I'll get you another one.

18
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:36,200
You turned out so well, my daughter.

19
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:41,467
Now that I see you,
you look just like your late mom.

20
00:03:43,933 --> 00:03:46,600
For seven years in prison,

21
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:50,467
I stared at the ceiling every night,
filled with regret.

22
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:53,467
That day...

23
00:03:58,733 --> 00:04:02,067
I should've killed you too.

24
00:04:02,767 --> 00:04:04,833
- Let go!
- You ungrateful brat!

25
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:06,967
After everything I did for you,
you reported your own dad?

26
00:04:06,967 --> 00:04:11,167
Do you have any idea how long
I've been waiting for this day?

27
00:04:13,933 --> 00:04:15,800
You little...

28
00:04:18,304 --> 00:04:19,844
You brat.

29
00:04:21,033 --> 00:04:23,000
Where do you think you're going?

30
00:04:24,733 --> 00:04:28,000
I'll finish what I should've done back then.

31
00:04:30,048 --> 00:04:31,808
You little brat.

32
00:04:34,167 --> 00:04:36,800
Get over here. Get over here!

33
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:48,100
Stay still, you punk.

34
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,733
The more you struggle,
the harder it'll be on you.

35
00:04:49,733 --> 00:04:51,624
Relax...

36
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:56,500
It's time for you to go meet your mom too.

37
00:05:44,733 --> 00:05:47,600
[Machine Wash]

38
00:06:21,112 --> 00:06:22,112
[Merry Christmas]

39
00:06:22,112 --> 00:06:25,033
Do you want a Christmas present?

40
00:06:26,233 --> 00:06:28,467
Then no crying.

41
00:06:30,067 --> 00:06:32,433
You have to be good.

42
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:36,992
I heard that Santa is very clear
about right and wrong.

43
00:06:36,992 --> 00:06:38,633
Miss, who are you?

44
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:43,200
Leave the living room window
slightly open when you get home.

45
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:45,300
And leave the lights on.

46
00:06:52,033 --> 00:06:53,700
See you again.

47
00:07:42,867 --> 00:07:48,647
[15 Years Later, Present Day]

48
00:08:03,867 --> 00:08:06,667
Mommy, wake up!

49
00:08:06,667 --> 00:08:08,500
Yul, you're awake?

50
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:10,100
Daddy, wake up too!

51
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:11,933
Five more minutes, just five...

52
00:08:11,933 --> 00:08:15,933
No, you have to go to work!

53
00:08:16,667 --> 00:08:20,300
Yul really takes after you,
no doubt about it.

54
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:23,233
Jeez, she's listening.

55
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:27,733
My Yul, you're so smart
because you take after your daddy.

56
00:08:27,733 --> 00:08:29,633
Are you awake?

57
00:08:29,633 --> 00:08:31,433
Really?

58
00:08:31,433 --> 00:08:33,567
Are you so smart
because you take after me, Yul?

59
00:08:33,567 --> 00:08:34,667
Yul, come here!

60
00:08:34,667 --> 00:08:37,167
Daddy, get up already.

61
00:08:37,167 --> 00:08:41,100
Oh, my little precious. Come here.

62
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,000
Yul, did you sleep well?

63
00:08:43,733 --> 00:08:45,760
I think we put her to bed too early.

64
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:49,900
Well, who was it that insisted
on putting her to bed so early?

65
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:51,767
Was that me?

66
00:08:53,067 --> 00:08:55,633
Then our big precious too...

67
00:08:55,633 --> 00:08:57,767
I need to go potty.

68
00:08:57,767 --> 00:09:00,033
- Potty...
- Let's go potty.

69
00:09:00,033 --> 00:09:03,233
Come on. Let's go potty.

70
00:09:03,233 --> 00:09:06,200
Let's go! Let's go potty.

71
00:09:10,767 --> 00:09:13,767
[Episode 1]

72
00:09:27,933 --> 00:09:31,533
The monster's coming after you!
I'll catch you!

73
00:09:31,533 --> 00:09:36,960
Let's go! Yul, let's go! Come on!

74
00:09:43,567 --> 00:09:45,760
[Kwon Yul, Dad, Mom]

75
00:10:09,933 --> 00:10:11,367
All done! Let's go!

76
00:10:11,367 --> 00:10:13,100
Daddy! The swings!

77
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:15,533
The swings!

78
00:10:19,872 --> 00:10:21,472
Well, it's good, right?

79
00:10:22,133 --> 00:10:24,733
Four-year-olds can eat on their own, right?

80
00:10:24,733 --> 00:10:25,800
Yeah.

81
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:29,233
Go ahead, Yul. Try eating by yourself.

82
00:10:29,233 --> 00:10:32,000
Time for an important decision.

83
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:36,433
The selfish new look, bought with money
stashed away from my wife.

84
00:10:36,433 --> 00:10:40,167
Or the rebellious night out, lying about
working late and heading to the club.

85
00:10:40,167 --> 00:10:41,800
Which one?

86
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:45,216
The rebel look today?

87
00:10:45,216 --> 00:10:47,967
Oh, my! Really?

88
00:10:47,967 --> 00:10:51,167
Wow, my wife is so generous.

89
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:55,733
When was the last time I went clubbing?

90
00:10:57,167 --> 00:10:58,967
Yul, did you eat it all by yourself?

91
00:10:58,967 --> 00:11:01,333
Awesome! You can eat all by yourself now!

92
00:11:01,333 --> 00:11:04,867
Daddy! Yul finished all her food.

93
00:11:04,867 --> 00:11:07,733
Really? You ate it all by yourself?

94
00:11:09,033 --> 00:11:10,967
That's amazing, my girl!

95
00:11:10,967 --> 00:11:12,900
What time is it? Oh, time to get dressed.

96
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:14,100
Let's go!

97
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:17,000
Let's go, let's go! Let's get you changed.

98
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,700
Honey, her P.E. uniform is over there.

99
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,000
Yul, do you have P.E. today?

100
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,233
- Yeah.
- That's nice.

101
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:23,533
- What time is it?
- Okay, then,

102
00:11:23,533 --> 00:11:25,833
stand on one foot for five seconds.

103
00:11:25,833 --> 00:11:27,100
Start!

104
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:28,700
One, two, three, four, five!

105
00:11:29,467 --> 00:11:31,200
Success!

106
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,867
- Success!
- Success!

107
00:11:33,867 --> 00:11:36,800
- One, two, three!
- One, two, three!

108
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:39,667
- One, two, three!
- One more time. One, two, three!

109
00:11:39,667 --> 00:11:42,233
Have fun with your friends. See you tonight!

110
00:11:42,233 --> 00:11:44,544
- Okay! Bye-bye!
- Bye-bye!

111
00:11:44,544 --> 00:11:45,867
Here.

112
00:11:48,233 --> 00:11:49,433
What?

113
00:11:49,433 --> 00:11:53,920
I feel like I had an important reason
to get off work early today.

114
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:55,833
What was it?

115
00:11:59,333 --> 00:12:01,733
Seriously, what was it?

116
00:12:01,733 --> 00:12:03,933
Well, what could it be?

117
00:12:05,733 --> 00:12:07,433
You're not falling for it, huh?

118
00:12:08,967 --> 00:12:13,833
I'll be home early today.
For my honey's big day tomorrow.

119
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:16,067
Oh, stop it.

120
00:12:17,133 --> 00:12:20,867
But if you'd forgotten,
you would've been in big trouble.

121
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:23,567
I really hope not.

122
00:12:23,567 --> 00:12:25,367
Right.

123
00:12:26,367 --> 00:12:31,400
Ms. Yoo Bo Na, have a great day today.
And I'll see you this evening.

124
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,033
Alright.

125
00:12:33,767 --> 00:12:35,200
What about what we didn't do earlier?

126
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,800
Now!

127
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,300
I'll get going. Bye-bye.

128
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:39,800
- Bye!
- Me too!

129
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:40,833
A kiss for Yul too!

130
00:12:40,833 --> 00:12:43,067
A kiss for Yul too! Bye!

131
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:44,067
Bye-bye!

132
00:12:44,067 --> 00:12:45,233
- See you later.
- Have a good day!

133
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:47,833
- I'll get going.
- Yul, I'm closing the door.

134
00:12:51,167 --> 00:12:53,533
♪ Baby shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪

135
00:12:53,533 --> 00:12:56,384
♪ Yul shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪

136
00:12:56,384 --> 00:12:58,900
♪ Mommy shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪

137
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:01,267
♪ Daddy shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪

138
00:13:01,267 --> 00:13:02,867
♪ Grandma ♪

139
00:13:05,267 --> 00:13:07,533
♪ Doo, doo, doo, doo ♪

140
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,067
Yul, shall we sing the song again?

141
00:13:23,067 --> 00:13:27,267
♪ Daddy shark, doo, doo, doo, doo ♪

142
00:13:27,267 --> 00:13:31,133
Yes, yes. Don't run! Be careful, careful!

143
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:33,500
- Goodbye!
- Yeah, yeah.

144
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,633
Take care.

145
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:36,800
Seo Jun!

146
00:13:37,467 --> 00:13:38,467
Up you go.

147
00:13:38,467 --> 00:13:39,767
Please take good care of him today.

148
00:13:39,767 --> 00:13:41,300
Be sure to listen to your teacher, okay?

149
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:43,367
- I'll be off.
- Okay, have a good day, Ma'am.

150
00:13:43,367 --> 00:13:45,167
- Hello!
- Hello!

151
00:13:46,067 --> 00:13:47,400
Hello.

152
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,633
Hello!

153
00:13:49,633 --> 00:13:51,733
- Hello.
- Hello!

154
00:13:51,733 --> 00:13:55,400
She always looks so relaxed. It's nice.

155
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:56,433
- Yul, you're here!
- Hello.

156
00:13:56,433 --> 00:13:58,933
Miss, I ate breakfast all by myself today.

157
00:13:58,933 --> 00:14:02,467
Oh, really? You did a great job.

158
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:04,133
Yul, say hello to your teacher first.

159
00:14:04,133 --> 00:14:07,567
- Give her a nice big bow.
- Good morning.

160
00:14:07,567 --> 00:14:09,200
Please take good care of her today too.

161
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:12,133
Don't worry. Yul seems to have adjusted now.

162
00:14:12,133 --> 00:14:15,233
Totally different from the beginning,
she's playing well and doing great.

163
00:14:15,233 --> 00:14:17,633
That's thanks to you. Thank you.

164
00:14:17,633 --> 00:14:19,633
Yul, shall we say goodbye to Mommy today?

165
00:14:19,633 --> 00:14:21,500
Okay. My Yul.

166
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,333
- Today, too, with friends,
- Today, too, with friends,

167
00:14:23,333 --> 00:14:25,233
- get along well!
- get along well!

168
00:14:25,233 --> 00:14:26,833
- Have a nice day!
- Yul, let's go.

169
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:28,067
Have a good day, Ma'am. See you later.

170
00:14:28,067 --> 00:14:31,333
- Okay.
- Yul's mom!

171
00:14:31,333 --> 00:14:34,100
How about a morning coffee for a change?

172
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:35,733
That sounds great.

173
00:14:36,967 --> 00:14:41,400
Oh, Ye Geon's mom,
did you not sleep well last night?

174
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:44,000
My kid dozed off poorly
in the early evening, woke up,

175
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,433
and then couldn't fall back asleep
until late at night.

176
00:14:46,433 --> 00:14:48,300
- Oh, dear, really?
- See?

177
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:50,000
I told you, right?

178
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,033
That's why you need to
stick to a daily routine.

179
00:14:53,033 --> 00:14:55,733
Otherwise, you'll end up twice as exhausted.

180
00:14:55,733 --> 00:15:02,184
Look at me. No matter how tired I am,
I never let my kid nap during the day.

181
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,867
Right, naps...

182
00:15:04,867 --> 00:15:08,167
By the way, isn't Seo Jun's mom amazing?

183
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:12,200
I saw earlier that she even seemed
to forget that today was P.E. day.

184
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:16,400
I don't know how she manages
to work while raising a child.

185
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:21,567
I'll... I'll go get it. You stay here.

186
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:27,100
How can you say that
after seeing that poor child earlier?

187
00:15:30,167 --> 00:15:34,533
If you can't do both properly,
you should just focus on one thing.

188
00:15:34,533 --> 00:15:35,667
Oh, dear.

189
00:15:35,667 --> 00:15:38,600
I just feel sorry for her.

190
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,480
Oh, well.

191
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,567
Thank you!

192
00:15:41,567 --> 00:15:43,467
The latte...

193
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:47,400
Still, I envy Seo Jun's mom sometimes.

194
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:50,767
It's hard, but at least
she gets to keep working.

195
00:15:50,767 --> 00:15:54,733
I only planned to take a short break,
but sometimes I regret staying home.

196
00:15:54,733 --> 00:15:55,767
Me too.

197
00:15:55,767 --> 00:16:00,333
After spending all day dealing with my kid,
I sometimes miss working outside too.

198
00:16:00,333 --> 00:16:02,500
Who wouldn't want to keep working?

199
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:05,767
Is there anyone here
who doesn't want to work?

200
00:16:05,767 --> 00:16:08,200
That's why I call it being greedy.

201
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:10,833
Kids need so much attention at that age.

202
00:16:10,833 --> 00:16:14,433
How can you leave them and work?

203
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:16,600
Is it really impossible?

204
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,600
Is it really that hard to work
while raising a child?

205
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:23,133
I really hope not...

206
00:16:23,133 --> 00:16:25,100
Why?

207
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:27,733
I'm going back to work starting tomorrow.

208
00:16:27,733 --> 00:16:28,733
Oh, my.

209
00:16:28,733 --> 00:16:35,067
My parental leave ends today,
so I'm going back to work tomorrow...

210
00:16:35,067 --> 00:16:38,300
Wait, you were a working mom this whole time?

211
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:41,267
How did we not know?

212
00:16:41,267 --> 00:16:45,300
What, so you were just
taking a break from work?

213
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:46,867
How long were you off work?

214
00:16:46,867 --> 00:16:49,700
- One year?
- Three years.

215
00:16:50,433 --> 00:16:52,633
I wanted to wait until my child
was a little older before going back...

216
00:16:52,633 --> 00:16:54,433
Three years? Are you a civil servant?

217
00:16:54,433 --> 00:16:56,300
Or do you work for a major company?

218
00:16:56,300 --> 00:16:59,500
No, I just work for a small company.

219
00:17:00,167 --> 00:17:02,167
A small company.

220
00:17:02,167 --> 00:17:03,967
Small...

221
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:11,333
I really enjoyed having
morning coffee together like this,

222
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:14,533
and learning parenting tips from you all.

223
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:17,233
And the coffee here is so delicious, right?

224
00:17:32,867 --> 00:17:35,300
Today is D-Day. Soryong Nightclub, Musan.

225
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:39,967
Today? Why does it have to be today?

226
00:17:40,933 --> 00:17:45,167
This won't do. This is a problem.

227
00:17:45,167 --> 00:17:47,500
I'm really in trouble now. Oh, my.

228
00:17:49,133 --> 00:17:52,633
Honey, I'm sorry. Really.
But this D-day was scheduled first...

229
00:17:52,633 --> 00:17:55,533
I'll really make it up to you.

230
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:04,200
[Mother]

231
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:06,720
Mother? Yes.

232
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:09,504
Yeah, it's fine. Go ahead.

233
00:18:11,733 --> 00:18:13,467
It must be a great company.

234
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:16,033
It's not easy to take the full three years
of parental leave.

235
00:18:16,033 --> 00:18:19,233
Or maybe she's just really capable?

236
00:18:19,233 --> 00:18:23,167
Well, she's been off for three years.
Why bother going back now...

237
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:26,633
I got it!

238
00:18:26,633 --> 00:18:27,700
What is it?

239
00:18:27,700 --> 00:18:29,700
The husband must be
struggling financially, I guess.

240
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:32,900
- Oh, no.
- That must have been hard.

241
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,233
She never told us.

242
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:37,567
Well, she has to earn her own money, I guess.

243
00:18:39,267 --> 00:18:42,867
More than half of the drug cases
uncovered by police in recent months

244
00:18:42,867 --> 00:18:46,500
have involved people in their 20s and 30s.

245
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:50,467
New types of drugs, including
liquid marijuana, ketamine, and fentanyl,

246
00:18:50,467 --> 00:18:52,333
are reportedly spreading

247
00:18:52,333 --> 00:18:57,700
among ordinary office workers and students
through clubs and private academies.

248
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:05,767
Mother, I'm here! Hello, Sister-in-law.

249
00:19:05,767 --> 00:19:08,567
Oh, my, you're here. What brings you here?

250
00:19:08,567 --> 00:19:10,833
I made some radish kimchi
that Tae Seong likes.

251
00:19:10,833 --> 00:19:13,100
Oh, radish kimchi?

252
00:19:14,467 --> 00:19:17,600
Let me get that, Mother. Just leave it.

253
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:21,200
Wow, it looks so appetizing
just from the sight of it.

254
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:25,300
My mom sure has all kinds of excuses
to call her daughter-in-law over.

255
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:27,800
Will my son even eat properly
starting tomorrow?

256
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,667
Don't worry, Mother.
I'll make sure he eats well.

257
00:19:30,667 --> 00:19:32,933
No wonder you treat him
like your precious only son.

258
00:19:32,933 --> 00:19:35,133
I'm sure she'll take good care of him.

259
00:19:35,133 --> 00:19:39,067
These days, daughters-in-law don't really
like their mothers-in-law fussing over them.

260
00:19:39,067 --> 00:19:40,267
Is that so?

261
00:19:40,267 --> 00:19:42,700
No, Mother. I really appreciate it.

262
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:45,600
Thank you, Mother. We'll enjoy it.

263
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:51,233
No matter how busy I was,
I've never fed my family instant food.

264
00:19:51,233 --> 00:19:53,033
I'll keep that in mind, Mother.

265
00:19:53,033 --> 00:19:59,128
Speaking of which, Mother,
that soy-marinated crab, jellyfish salad,

266
00:19:59,128 --> 00:20:00,128
and pickled perilla leaves
you made last time,

267
00:20:00,128 --> 00:20:02,367
could you make them again?

268
00:20:03,167 --> 00:20:05,300
- Huh?
- Tae Seong really loved them.

269
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,933
We finished them in less than three days.

270
00:20:06,933 --> 00:20:09,167
Oh, sure, I'll make them.

271
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:11,367
Really? Thank you.

272
00:20:11,367 --> 00:20:13,167
Is there anything
I can help you with, Mother?

273
00:20:13,167 --> 00:20:17,167
Oh, no, just go quickly.
You probably have a lot to prepare.

274
00:20:17,167 --> 00:20:18,333
- No, it's fine.
- Oh, my.

275
00:20:18,333 --> 00:20:21,800
Why does my shoulder hurt so much today?

276
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,267
- When am I going to finish all this...
- Mother, leave it.

277
00:20:23,267 --> 00:20:25,767
- I'll do it. Leave it.
- Mother!

278
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:33,967
Okay, let's do this.

279
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:45,867
Oh, Mom, really...

280
00:20:45,867 --> 00:20:49,367
Do you really have to work her
on her last day off?

281
00:20:49,367 --> 00:20:52,233
I'm not making her do anything.
She offered to do it.

282
00:20:52,233 --> 00:20:53,633
Oh, dear.

283
00:20:53,633 --> 00:20:55,900
- What?
- Oh, hello.

284
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:57,767
Is your daughter-in-law
going back to work tomorrow?

285
00:20:57,767 --> 00:20:59,700
She's returning to work or something.

286
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:02,267
Oh! That's good.

287
00:21:02,267 --> 00:21:05,833
It's hard to make a living on
one income these days.

288
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:08,867
My son has been working himself
to the bone supporting the family alone.

289
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:10,533
So, was she just sitting around
all this time?

290
00:21:10,533 --> 00:21:14,433
Jeez, I'm sure her salary
is barely anything anyway.

291
00:21:14,433 --> 00:21:15,867
She's already acting all high and mighty.

292
00:21:15,867 --> 00:21:17,500
Mom!

293
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:19,600
When did she ever act like that?

294
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:23,767
Didn't you say your daughter-in-law
worked for some big company?

295
00:21:23,767 --> 00:21:25,800
Was it some place
that sells refrigerators and TVs?

296
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,967
You're talking nonsense.

297
00:21:27,967 --> 00:21:31,300
That one. She works for that fan company.

298
00:21:34,033 --> 00:21:35,400
I need to replace my fan.

299
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:37,967
Can you get an employee discount
or something?

300
00:21:37,967 --> 00:21:40,200
They probably don't make much money
selling those anyway.

301
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:42,400
Anyway, why are you here?

302
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,633
- Did you hear?
- Hear what?

303
00:21:43,633 --> 00:21:48,067
That Chinese restaurant in the front
shopping area is closing down.

304
00:21:48,067 --> 00:21:51,533
What? Isn't that the place
where people line up to eat?

305
00:21:51,533 --> 00:21:52,800
Why are they suddenly closing?

306
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:56,300
Apparently the building owner
tripled the rent.

307
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,233
- Oh, my.
- What else could it mean?

308
00:21:58,233 --> 00:21:59,233
They're telling them to leave.

309
00:21:59,233 --> 00:22:01,367
Wow, that's really nasty.

310
00:22:01,367 --> 00:22:04,800
Since business is good, they want to
open their own restaurant there.

311
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,800
[Tae Seong Chicken]

312
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:22,848
[Big sale today:
30% off select industrial products]

313
00:22:22,848 --> 00:22:24,833
[50% off all agricultural products]
Oh, the mart is having a sale.

314
00:22:44,633 --> 00:22:47,267
At least I've been lucky with my landlord.

315
00:22:47,267 --> 00:22:49,733
The rent for all the shops around here
goes up every year,

316
00:22:49,733 --> 00:22:52,133
but mine has stayed the same for five years.

317
00:22:52,133 --> 00:22:53,867
It'll probably stay that way
this time too, right?

318
00:22:53,867 --> 00:22:54,867
I guess so.

319
00:22:54,867 --> 00:22:58,633
Oh! Oh, my gosh! You're being too naive.

320
00:22:58,633 --> 00:23:00,833
How can you be so sure
about someone's intentions?

321
00:23:00,833 --> 00:23:04,800
After five years frozen, they could raise it
all at once, and we'd have no say.

322
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:07,100
Oh, no way!

323
00:23:07,100 --> 00:23:10,200
Business isn't even good these days.

324
00:23:21,367 --> 00:23:22,933
If you're really worried,

325
00:23:22,933 --> 00:23:26,467
you should visit the landlord beforehand
and show some appreciation.

326
00:23:26,467 --> 00:23:29,300
Who could say no to a smiling face?

327
00:23:33,967 --> 00:23:37,133
Sun Il, let's go buy a gift right now.

328
00:23:37,133 --> 00:23:40,500
The landlord must be loaded.
What are you going to buy?

329
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:41,733
I guess you're right.

330
00:23:41,733 --> 00:23:43,500
What should we buy, then?

331
00:23:44,267 --> 00:23:45,633
Ask your daughter-in-law.

332
00:23:45,633 --> 00:23:49,133
Young moms usually
have a better sense for these things.

333
00:23:49,133 --> 00:23:51,567
What sense? My foot.

334
00:23:51,567 --> 00:23:55,500
She showed up empty-handed
the first time she came to meet

335
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:56,867
her future mother-in-law.

336
00:23:56,867 --> 00:24:00,800
One time, I asked her to buy
some red ginseng as a gift,

337
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:03,967
and she brought back
a whole fresh ginseng root instead.

338
00:24:03,967 --> 00:24:06,900
Come on, no way!

339
00:24:09,900 --> 00:24:12,500
My sister-in-law is just a little unusual.

340
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:15,433
Sometimes she just doesn't know things
everyone else does.

341
00:24:15,433 --> 00:24:17,133
Really?

342
00:24:20,133 --> 00:24:21,967
Well, that's probably
because she's an orphan.

343
00:24:21,967 --> 00:24:25,600
She didn't have parents
to learn those things from.

344
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:27,500
Bye.

345
00:24:28,467 --> 00:24:31,167
Oh, what do you mean help?

346
00:24:31,167 --> 00:24:34,600
She couldn't even stick around and ran off...

347
00:24:38,500 --> 00:24:41,800
When did she chop all of this?

348
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:44,067
Look at how even they are.

349
00:24:44,067 --> 00:24:47,333
How can this...

350
00:24:47,333 --> 00:24:49,300
I'm scared.

351
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:51,300
- What's this?
- What is going on?

352
00:24:51,300 --> 00:24:53,433
[Black Beans]

353
00:24:53,433 --> 00:24:54,533
Black beans...

354
00:24:54,533 --> 00:24:56,500
[Today Only: Unbeatable Price,
50% Off All Agricultural Products]

355
00:24:56,500 --> 00:24:59,233
- These onions are nice and big.
- They're so cheap.

356
00:24:59,233 --> 00:25:01,367
- The autumn squash is a good price.
- Oh, my.

357
00:25:01,367 --> 00:25:04,233
They're doing something over there too.
Let's go check it out.

358
00:25:12,067 --> 00:25:13,800
Miss Kim!

359
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:17,300
What are you doing after work?

360
00:25:17,300 --> 00:25:19,167
I asked what you're doing afterward.

361
00:25:19,167 --> 00:25:20,800
Why are you acting like this?

362
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:24,500
Come on, just stay a minute.
You like this, don't you?

363
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:26,500
Please don't do this.

364
00:25:28,367 --> 00:25:30,233
I'll get going now.

365
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:37,367
Who was that?

366
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:41,667
Miss Kim!

367
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:50,100
Oh, my back!

368
00:25:50,100 --> 00:25:51,833
[Trash Can Deodorizer]
Who did this?

369
00:25:51,833 --> 00:25:53,600
Who was it?

370
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,400
Oh, my.

371
00:26:00,067 --> 00:26:02,167
Now, for the next 30 minutes only,

372
00:26:02,167 --> 00:26:04,300
we're offering our seasonal
health-boosting samgyetang

373
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:07,700
at a special buy-one-get-one deal.

374
00:26:07,700 --> 00:26:09,900
Got the samgyetang!

375
00:26:20,233 --> 00:26:22,233
[Big Precious]

376
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:28,933
Honey, I love you!
I'll really make it up to you.

377
00:26:39,633 --> 00:26:43,467
Wow, my wife really saw it coming.

378
00:26:43,467 --> 00:26:46,267
[Musan Soryong Nightclub]

379
00:26:46,267 --> 00:26:48,900
Wait, get out. Get out.

380
00:26:48,900 --> 00:26:50,467
Come here. I need to wipe your feet.

381
00:26:50,467 --> 00:26:52,200
No, I don't want to!

382
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:54,500
Yul, come here! You have to wipe your feet.

383
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:56,400
You'll catch a cold. Hurry.

384
00:26:57,700 --> 00:27:00,633
Okay. Then stay right there.

385
00:27:10,700 --> 00:27:14,300
Honey, I'm in Musan right now.

386
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:17,733
Something urgent came up
for a business trip, so I might be late.

387
00:27:18,567 --> 00:27:22,733
I was supposed to get home early
and help you... I'm sorry.

388
00:27:22,733 --> 00:27:25,033
I'll take the last bus and come,
even if I'm late.

389
00:27:25,033 --> 00:27:26,933
I love you, Bo Na.

390
00:27:26,933 --> 00:27:29,067
You know how much I love you, right?

391
00:27:29,067 --> 00:27:31,533
Oh, this man, seriously...

392
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:42,733
Just wait until you get home.
You're not getting away with this.

393
00:27:42,733 --> 00:27:45,933
It can't be helped. It's okay.

394
00:27:45,933 --> 00:27:47,833
Take care of your work and don't worry.

395
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:50,000
Just stop sending those crying emojis.

396
00:27:56,467 --> 00:27:58,267
Yul, let's get dressed now!

397
00:27:58,267 --> 00:27:59,567
- Come here.
- No, I don't want to.

398
00:27:59,567 --> 00:28:00,567
Come here!

399
00:28:00,567 --> 00:28:02,600
- Come on, hurry.
- No!

400
00:28:02,600 --> 00:28:03,700
Come quickly.

401
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:06,567
Come here! Come here!

402
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:32,767
Boss, I'll just go use
the bathroom real quick.

403
00:29:32,767 --> 00:29:33,767
You punk!

404
00:29:33,767 --> 00:29:35,533
I'm sorry.

405
00:29:35,533 --> 00:29:37,133
Give it to me!

406
00:29:58,333 --> 00:30:00,633
[Empty Taxi]
Follow that black car, please.

407
00:30:02,867 --> 00:30:04,467
Let's sleep.

408
00:30:04,467 --> 00:30:07,367
I'm going to sleep with Daddy.
When's Daddy coming?

409
00:30:07,367 --> 00:30:10,200
I told you that Daddy is busy with work
and will be late today.

410
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:11,967
Sleep with me, okay?

411
00:30:11,967 --> 00:30:14,567
No, I'll sleep when Daddy gets home.

412
00:30:14,567 --> 00:30:17,233
Where did Daddy go?

413
00:30:17,233 --> 00:30:20,400
His work isn't finished yet.

414
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:22,800
Should I sing you a song?

415
00:30:22,800 --> 00:30:24,533
What kind of work?

416
00:30:26,267 --> 00:30:30,900
Daddy is doing...
something very, very important.

417
00:30:30,900 --> 00:30:36,467
He is a truly good man
who does wonderful things for people.

418
00:30:36,467 --> 00:30:38,433
A good person?

419
00:30:38,433 --> 00:30:44,600
Yes. A very good person
who makes the world brighter.

420
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:45,633
Yeah, honey.

421
00:30:45,633 --> 00:30:46,900
Honey, are you on your way?

422
00:30:46,900 --> 00:30:47,933
Yes, I'm on my way.

423
00:30:47,933 --> 00:30:50,467
I prepared the barbecue,
but I haven't picked out the wine yet.

424
00:30:50,467 --> 00:30:52,267
Barbecue with wine?

425
00:30:52,267 --> 00:30:54,700
Of course, Napa Cabernet.

426
00:30:54,700 --> 00:30:58,533
Napa Cabernet? Okay, I'll get that, then.

427
00:30:58,533 --> 00:31:00,500
How much longer?

428
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:12,133
How far is he going?

429
00:31:19,400 --> 00:31:21,400
Sir, I'm almost out of time
for the last train.

430
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:24,300
Is Musan Station far from here?
How long will it take?

431
00:31:24,300 --> 00:31:26,233
What, Musan Station?

432
00:31:41,033 --> 00:31:43,500
Oh, my, what happened here?

433
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:47,700
Ambulance...

434
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:50,367
- Call an ambulance. Now!
- Okay.

435
00:32:00,400 --> 00:32:05,033
Yes, hello. There's been
a vehicle explosion here.

436
00:32:12,133 --> 00:32:14,200
Rest in peace.

437
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:17,433
I can't tell you to be reborn.

438
00:32:42,033 --> 00:32:45,833
Yul, we're late! Yul, get out!

439
00:32:46,533 --> 00:32:49,333
Yul, what did I say today was?

440
00:32:49,333 --> 00:32:51,567
- Your first day back at work!
- Right?

441
00:32:51,567 --> 00:32:54,867
Then who did I say would pick you up
after daycare today?

442
00:32:54,867 --> 00:32:55,933
Ms. Hee Seon!

443
00:32:55,933 --> 00:32:59,000
Yul, our Yul! Why are you so smart?

444
00:33:00,867 --> 00:33:02,800
Let's go, let's go. Hurry.

445
00:33:04,067 --> 00:33:05,700
Hello, Miss!

446
00:33:05,700 --> 00:33:08,933
Oh, my, Yul is a little late today.

447
00:33:08,933 --> 00:33:10,267
You're starting today, right?

448
00:33:10,267 --> 00:33:13,733
Yes, so starting today,
a helper will be picking Yul up.

449
00:33:13,733 --> 00:33:15,633
But it's our first time,
both for me and Yul, so...

450
00:33:15,633 --> 00:33:17,024
Oh, don't worry too much.

451
00:33:17,024 --> 00:33:18,500
I'll keep a close eye on Yul

452
00:33:18,500 --> 00:33:20,133
and contact you right away
if anything happens.

453
00:33:20,133 --> 00:33:21,733
Thank you.

454
00:33:21,733 --> 00:33:23,700
Yul. My Yul.

455
00:33:23,700 --> 00:33:25,167
- Today, too...
- Today, too, with friends...

456
00:33:25,167 --> 00:33:26,867
Get along well!

457
00:33:26,867 --> 00:33:28,333
See you later.

458
00:33:28,333 --> 00:33:29,667
Have a great day, Ma'am. Let's go in.

459
00:33:29,667 --> 00:33:31,567
Mommy, bye-bye!

460
00:33:35,267 --> 00:33:37,184
[Child on Board]

461
00:33:43,900 --> 00:33:46,200
Okay, let's get going.

462
00:33:49,933 --> 00:33:54,833
Last night, a vehicle exploded on
an outer road in Musan while driving.

463
00:33:54,833 --> 00:33:58,300
The driver, a man in his 40s
identified as Mr. Bae, died at the scene.

464
00:33:58,300 --> 00:34:00,767
Police say they have asked the NFS
to analyze the crash vehicle

465
00:34:00,767 --> 00:34:06,567
and perform an autopsy to determine
the details of the brutal case.

466
00:34:06,567 --> 00:34:07,600
In other news,

467
00:34:07,600 --> 00:34:10,533
Hwang, who had been serving time
for allegedly murdering his pregnant wife,

468
00:34:10,533 --> 00:34:13,267
has been released after three years,
sparking controversy.

469
00:34:13,267 --> 00:34:16,433
Three years ago, Hwang caused
an accident while driving drunk

470
00:34:16,433 --> 00:34:21,300
and was arrested for killing
his pregnant wife in the passenger seat.

471
00:34:31,467 --> 00:34:33,200
What time is it now?

472
00:34:38,833 --> 00:34:42,200
Honey, I missed the last train.

473
00:34:42,200 --> 00:34:45,233
I have some additional reporting to do,
so I think I need to stay here one more day.

474
00:34:45,233 --> 00:34:47,633
I'm sorry.

475
00:34:47,633 --> 00:34:50,100
Just wait till you get home, Kwon Tae Seong.

476
00:34:58,900 --> 00:35:00,667
It's pretty.

477
00:35:01,933 --> 00:35:04,256
[Durumi Electronics]

478
00:35:09,867 --> 00:35:12,700
[Yoo Bo Na]

479
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:25,632
[Durumi Electronics]

480
00:35:37,533 --> 00:35:38,900
Excuse me...

481
00:35:38,900 --> 00:35:41,400
What are you doing? Aren't you going in?

482
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:45,033
Oh, this is so old.

483
00:35:45,033 --> 00:35:46,667
Excuse...

484
00:35:48,467 --> 00:35:50,336
I opened it temporarily for one day.

485
00:35:50,336 --> 00:35:52,567
You can get your new ID badge later.

486
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:54,200
Pretty good.

487
00:36:02,200 --> 00:36:04,067
Ki Yeong Do, it's been a while.

488
00:36:04,067 --> 00:36:05,967
I'm Assistant Manager Ki.

489
00:36:05,967 --> 00:36:08,033
- What?
- It's been a while since I got promoted.

490
00:36:08,033 --> 00:36:12,400
You got promoted?
Congratulations, Assistant Manager Ki.

491
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:13,600
You look great.

492
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:15,433
You haven't changed a bit either.

493
00:36:15,433 --> 00:36:17,667
Really? I couldn't sleep last night.

494
00:36:17,667 --> 00:36:19,867
Why couldn't you sleep?

495
00:36:20,900 --> 00:36:23,400
- Because I heard you were coming back.
- Here it is.

496
00:36:24,567 --> 00:36:26,167
Let's go!

497
00:36:31,233 --> 00:36:33,933
Welcome back!

498
00:36:37,600 --> 00:36:39,200
[Welcome Back, Director Yoo Bo Na]

499
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:40,667
You're finally back.

500
00:36:40,667 --> 00:36:44,133
Our Director Yoo Bo Na,
whom I've only heard about.

501
00:36:45,067 --> 00:36:46,833
Thank you.

502
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,900
This is Assistant Manager Yang Ye Sol,
who joined while you were away.

503
00:36:50,900 --> 00:36:53,533
She took over from Jeong In Joo.

504
00:36:53,533 --> 00:36:55,333
I've heard so much about you.

505
00:36:55,333 --> 00:36:57,233
I heard you used to be the best on our team.

506
00:36:57,233 --> 00:37:00,700
I've seriously been waiting forever
to meet you.

507
00:37:00,700 --> 00:37:03,933
Not because of your performance or anything.

508
00:37:03,933 --> 00:37:07,500
Anyway, it's really great
to finally meet you.

509
00:37:07,500 --> 00:37:10,600
It's so good to meet you too.

510
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:15,833
Manager Go, you've been
doing well too, right?

511
00:37:15,833 --> 00:37:17,567
Oh, yeah.

512
00:37:17,567 --> 00:37:20,100
You're finally back, Director Yoo.

513
00:37:21,967 --> 00:37:24,133
I'll head to my desk.

514
00:37:37,867 --> 00:37:39,367
Is the team leader not here yet?

515
00:37:39,367 --> 00:37:41,967
Oh, he went on a business trip
to Musan yesterday.

516
00:37:41,967 --> 00:37:44,167
He got back early this morning,
so he'll be a little late.

517
00:37:44,167 --> 00:37:46,067
Musan?

518
00:37:46,067 --> 00:37:48,200
Oh, I see.

519
00:37:50,167 --> 00:37:52,367
Is he still the same?

520
00:37:52,367 --> 00:37:54,267
Still the same.

521
00:37:54,267 --> 00:37:55,567
You're here?

522
00:37:55,567 --> 00:37:58,833
- You're here?
- Hi! Good morning!

523
00:37:58,833 --> 00:38:00,567
You swept the market again, huh?

524
00:38:00,567 --> 00:38:02,633
What is it this time, Team Leader?

525
00:38:04,967 --> 00:38:08,967
Lettuce. Look how fresh it is.

526
00:38:08,967 --> 00:38:10,733
Ms. Yoo Bo Na is here.

527
00:38:10,733 --> 00:38:12,367
What?

528
00:38:13,533 --> 00:38:15,333
Director Yoo!

529
00:38:20,900 --> 00:38:24,000
Wow, how long has it been?

530
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:27,600
You're finally back! Our team's ace.

531
00:38:27,600 --> 00:38:30,367
Have you been well?

532
00:38:30,367 --> 00:38:32,833
You're still the same, Team Leader.

533
00:38:34,600 --> 00:38:40,067
Wow, with Director Yoo back,
the office feels full and lively.

534
00:38:40,067 --> 00:38:44,000
A person needs to have some presence.

535
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:49,100
Oh, right. We'll catch up properly
when we have the time and money.

536
00:38:49,100 --> 00:38:53,533
But today, I have something
urgent on my mind.

537
00:38:55,133 --> 00:38:57,000
Welcome back.

538
00:38:58,933 --> 00:39:01,333
Alright, get back to work!

539
00:39:04,367 --> 00:39:07,733
[Musan City Police Station]

540
00:39:08,544 --> 00:39:09,632
[A Safe, Clean Sea of Hope]

541
00:39:23,933 --> 00:39:26,800
Excuse me, excuse me!

542
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:29,467
I heard you were at the scene.
May I have your name?

543
00:39:29,467 --> 00:39:32,167
Oh, yes. Just a moment.

544
00:39:33,700 --> 00:39:36,933
I'm Kwon Tae Seong, a reporter
from Digging Deep News, Not Today.

545
00:39:36,933 --> 00:39:38,400
[Not Today Reporter, Kwon Tae Seong]
What's your name, sir?

546
00:39:38,400 --> 00:39:43,000
Well, what brings an investigative reporter
all the way from Seoul to Musan?

547
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:44,800
Has the victim's identity been confirmed yet?

548
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:47,833
What on earth is going on here?

549
00:39:47,833 --> 00:39:49,767
I think that's something
I should be asking you.

550
00:39:49,767 --> 00:39:51,967
So what exactly happened here?

551
00:39:51,967 --> 00:39:53,100
Excuse me?

552
00:39:53,100 --> 00:39:55,167
Well, the taxi driver said

553
00:39:55,167 --> 00:39:58,733
you came out of a club
and suddenly asked him to follow this car.

554
00:39:58,733 --> 00:40:00,367
So, what was that about?

555
00:40:00,367 --> 00:40:03,267
Well, what else would a reporter be doing?
I was covering a story.

556
00:40:03,267 --> 00:40:04,267
Like I am now.

557
00:40:04,267 --> 00:40:06,933
A story? What kind of story?

558
00:40:09,133 --> 00:40:12,733
We received information that a new type
of drug had infiltrated clubs around Musan.

559
00:40:12,733 --> 00:40:15,533
So I was meeting an informant today
for an interview, when...

560
00:40:15,533 --> 00:40:18,233
Oh, then what about the car?

561
00:40:18,233 --> 00:40:20,300
Why did you follow it?

562
00:40:22,500 --> 00:40:25,467
Am I a witness? A person of interest?

563
00:40:26,100 --> 00:40:27,533
Or am I a suspect?

564
00:40:27,533 --> 00:40:30,767
No, it's not like that.
Just tell me what happened...

565
00:40:30,767 --> 00:40:32,967
The informant said that man was a dropper.

566
00:40:32,967 --> 00:40:34,933
- A dropper?
- I was following him

567
00:40:34,933 --> 00:40:39,100
in case I could catch him
distributing drugs to other clubs.

568
00:40:39,100 --> 00:40:40,800
Drug-related reports

569
00:40:40,800 --> 00:40:45,133
tend to focus sensationally
on ordinary users consuming drugs.

570
00:40:45,133 --> 00:40:48,433
But I wanted to focus on the suppliers

571
00:40:48,433 --> 00:40:50,533
and expose how these drugs are distributed.

572
00:40:50,533 --> 00:40:52,533
I thought it could raise public awareness

573
00:40:52,533 --> 00:40:57,267
and also help your investigations
and arrests in making society safer.

574
00:40:57,267 --> 00:40:58,900
Does that answer your question?

575
00:40:59,967 --> 00:41:02,533
Oh, yeah. That's admirable.

576
00:41:02,533 --> 00:41:06,667
But if he's a dropper, isn't he just
a low-level errand boy who delivers drugs?

577
00:41:06,667 --> 00:41:10,833
Oh, dear, Mr. Reporter,
I guess you've got the wrong idea.

578
00:41:10,833 --> 00:41:13,300
- Pardon?
- For now, go home.

579
00:41:13,300 --> 00:41:14,688
We may contact you later
for a witness interview,

580
00:41:14,688 --> 00:41:17,233
so please be aware of that.

581
00:41:17,233 --> 00:41:20,033
As you can see,
the scene is a mess right now. I'm off.

582
00:41:20,033 --> 00:41:23,900
Please make sure you take
thorough photos of the scene.

583
00:41:25,867 --> 00:41:27,700
[Son Seok Gu]

584
00:41:34,033 --> 00:41:35,033
- Hello...
- Why do you keep calling?

585
00:41:35,033 --> 00:41:36,167
You're putting me in a difficult position.

586
00:41:36,167 --> 00:41:38,800
I've called you several times.
Why haven't you answered?

587
00:41:38,800 --> 00:41:42,367
I need to see you right now. Where are you?

588
00:41:42,367 --> 00:41:45,667
Meet? What for? It's chaos here
because of what happened.

589
00:41:45,667 --> 00:41:47,700
Don't contact me again.
I'm changing my number.

590
00:41:47,700 --> 00:41:50,767
Wait, hold on! Let me ask you just one thing.

591
00:41:50,767 --> 00:41:54,000
What happened to that dropper from yesterday?

592
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:56,700
Why are you asking about him?

593
00:41:56,700 --> 00:42:00,467
He came back shortly
after you left yesterday.

594
00:42:00,467 --> 00:42:01,800
- Well, then...
- I'm hanging up.

595
00:42:01,800 --> 00:42:03,400
Hello...

596
00:42:18,467 --> 00:42:20,467
That persistent guy actually showed up.

597
00:42:20,467 --> 00:42:24,000
I told you over the phone
several times that it's not possible.

598
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:25,667
Who was the victim in last night's incident?

599
00:42:25,667 --> 00:42:28,567
Jeez, what kind of reporter is so pushy...

600
00:42:32,267 --> 00:42:35,400
I'm the one who witnessed
the scene firsthand. Look at me.

601
00:42:35,400 --> 00:42:36,800
I still feel sick to my stomach.

602
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:41,133
Well, if you feel sick, you can go to
a pharmacy and get some medicine.

603
00:42:41,133 --> 00:42:42,733
I even betrayed my wife.

604
00:42:42,733 --> 00:42:47,167
I was supposed to get home
no matter what yesterday.

605
00:42:47,167 --> 00:42:49,533
Then hurry home now.

606
00:42:49,533 --> 00:42:51,733
Come on, it's already too late.

607
00:42:51,733 --> 00:42:55,300
Today was my wife's first day back at work.

608
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:57,367
Sir, are you married? My daughter is four.

609
00:42:57,367 --> 00:43:01,333
Why are you telling me
your daughter is four right now?

610
00:43:01,333 --> 00:43:03,500
I mean, it's not really relevant...

611
00:43:03,500 --> 00:43:06,300
Anyway, the victim, Mr. Bae,
is the drug kingpin Bae Doo Hyuk, right?

612
00:43:06,300 --> 00:43:09,033
Well, that's true, but...

613
00:43:10,767 --> 00:43:13,067
Come on.

614
00:43:13,067 --> 00:43:17,152
Was this just an accident?
Or... was it possibly murder?

615
00:43:20,096 --> 00:43:21,233
Come out.

616
00:43:21,233 --> 00:43:22,500
- Is that right?
- Come out!

617
00:43:22,500 --> 00:43:23,567
Please just tell me once.

618
00:43:23,567 --> 00:43:25,700
I said come out. Come out.

619
00:43:25,700 --> 00:43:28,633
- Well, Director Yoo.
- Yes?

620
00:43:28,633 --> 00:43:31,267
I feel bad asking this
on your first day back,

621
00:43:31,267 --> 00:43:35,667
but today, could you do a client meeting?

622
00:43:37,367 --> 00:43:38,633
Today, right away?

623
00:43:38,633 --> 00:43:40,100
Yeah, today.

624
00:43:40,100 --> 00:43:41,900
I know it's a lot to ask on your first day.

625
00:43:41,900 --> 00:43:44,933
And I know you're not someone
who does things halfway.

626
00:43:44,933 --> 00:43:49,167
But the client said today is
the only time they can make it.

627
00:43:49,167 --> 00:43:52,233
Assistant Manager Ki prepared everything.

628
00:43:53,933 --> 00:43:58,000
You just need to handle the meeting.

629
00:43:58,000 --> 00:43:59,200
[Client Report]

630
00:44:13,833 --> 00:44:15,333
You prepared everything thoroughly.

631
00:44:15,333 --> 00:44:17,433
I learned well from you.

632
00:44:20,833 --> 00:44:22,700
Let's do it during the day.

633
00:44:23,833 --> 00:44:25,167
During the day? Why?

634
00:44:25,167 --> 00:44:28,333
Considering the meeting location
and the client's schedule,

635
00:44:28,333 --> 00:44:30,033
having thought about it in detail,

636
00:44:30,033 --> 00:44:34,133
do you think it's strategically better
to do it during the day, Director Yoo?

637
00:44:34,133 --> 00:44:36,533
I have to pick up my kid.

638
00:44:38,500 --> 00:44:40,700
My husband is going to be late today.

639
00:44:44,300 --> 00:44:47,167
Let's do it during the day.

640
00:44:50,567 --> 00:44:53,472
[Client Information]

641
00:44:59,367 --> 00:45:04,000
Whether it's an accident or murder,
we'll know after the NFS results come out.

642
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:07,767
And I wasn't the one who told you
the victim's name, okay?

643
00:45:15,520 --> 00:45:17,333
[A Safe, Clean Sea of Hope]

644
00:45:17,333 --> 00:45:19,867
Please take me to
the Musan Forensic Science Institute.

645
00:45:45,567 --> 00:45:48,033
I like the meeting venue.

646
00:45:49,267 --> 00:45:52,000
The client arrived an hour ago
and is waiting inside.

647
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:53,000
You can go right in.

648
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:55,367
Okay, let's see what you've got.

649
00:45:55,367 --> 00:45:57,367
Me?

650
00:45:57,367 --> 00:45:58,633
Oh, come on. Of course, I...

651
00:45:58,633 --> 00:46:00,767
Not you, me.

652
00:46:01,767 --> 00:46:03,833
Are you nervous?

653
00:46:03,833 --> 00:46:06,700
Well, I guess it has been a while.

654
00:46:06,700 --> 00:46:08,467
That's true for you.

655
00:46:08,467 --> 00:46:10,467
Stop shaking your leg.

656
00:46:24,167 --> 00:46:26,933
You too, Team Leader. Relax your grip.

657
00:46:47,840 --> 00:46:48,900
[Please Hear Our Prayer]

658
00:46:48,900 --> 00:46:50,733
Have you ever prayed?

659
00:46:50,733 --> 00:46:53,000
Of course not. What about you?

660
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:56,800
Sometimes, without realizing it,
during moments that really shake me.

661
00:46:58,967 --> 00:47:02,500
You have moments like that too? When?

662
00:47:02,500 --> 00:47:06,767
When the child is chewing on
something and eating.

663
00:47:26,867 --> 00:47:29,000
Isn't it a good thing if the child eats well?

664
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:31,467
The problem is that I never gave
the child anything to eat.

665
00:47:31,467 --> 00:47:34,033
Nothing has ever scared me
more than that moment.

666
00:47:43,467 --> 00:47:46,667
You should see a long bench
in the right corner.

667
00:47:46,667 --> 00:47:48,300
Yeah, I see it.

668
00:47:50,533 --> 00:47:54,867
Do you know when it's hardest
to comfort a crying four-year-old?

669
00:47:54,867 --> 00:47:57,933
- When?
- When a friend gets hurt at daycare.

670
00:47:57,933 --> 00:48:00,267
Oh, out of sadness?

671
00:48:00,267 --> 00:48:05,133
No, guilt. She thought
it was her fault and cried for an hour.

672
00:48:05,133 --> 00:48:07,600
Come on, what does a four-year-old even know?

673
00:48:07,600 --> 00:48:09,833
They know. Even four-year-olds.

674
00:48:09,833 --> 00:48:10,867
What?

675
00:48:10,867 --> 00:48:15,600
They know that they shouldn't
hurt someone, even by accident.

676
00:48:17,567 --> 00:48:19,500
Okay, shall we go?

677
00:48:22,067 --> 00:48:23,967
Now is a good time.

678
00:49:06,033 --> 00:49:10,533
Sales Team 3, Yoo Bo Na,
starting client meeting.

679
00:50:01,733 --> 00:50:03,600
Meeting concluded.

680
00:50:23,667 --> 00:50:25,833
Still got it.

681
00:50:41,200 --> 00:50:43,333
Rest in peace.

682
00:50:44,900 --> 00:50:48,033
I can't tell you to be reborn.

683
00:51:08,200 --> 00:51:10,867
Yoo Bo Na comes back.

684
00:51:32,667 --> 00:51:35,900
- Yul.
- Mommy!

685
00:51:35,900 --> 00:51:37,500
Yul!

686
00:51:37,500 --> 00:51:39,700
- Chae Won, hello.
- Hello.

687
00:51:39,700 --> 00:51:42,267
Did you have fun playing with Chae Won today?

688
00:51:42,267 --> 00:51:44,733
Yeah, I made this with her.

689
00:51:44,733 --> 00:51:45,767
Mommy, it's a present for you!

690
00:51:45,767 --> 00:51:48,500
What is this? Is it a rose?

691
00:51:48,500 --> 00:51:49,600
Yeah.

692
00:51:49,600 --> 00:51:51,133
But it's not my birthday today.

693
00:51:51,133 --> 00:51:54,400
I told her you had a hard first day
back at work, and she made this.

694
00:51:54,400 --> 00:51:57,033
Oh, you did that, Yul?

695
00:51:57,033 --> 00:51:58,533
You like flowers.

696
00:51:58,533 --> 00:52:00,633
Yes, that's right! You're the best, Yul.

697
00:52:00,633 --> 00:52:03,067
My Yul is the best! Thank you.

698
00:52:03,067 --> 00:52:05,700
Let me see, Yul. It looks just like you.

699
00:52:05,700 --> 00:52:08,533
Oh, you're so cute.

700
00:52:08,533 --> 00:52:10,333
Thank you!

701
00:52:10,967 --> 00:52:13,000
Let's go home now, okay?

702
00:52:24,267 --> 00:52:26,767
What concept is this supposed to be?

703
00:52:26,767 --> 00:52:29,733
It's the kind of face you talk about
when you say someone has no shame.

704
00:52:29,733 --> 00:52:32,600
It's not funny at all. Stop it.

705
00:52:37,633 --> 00:52:39,467
Honey, I'm sorry...

706
00:52:39,467 --> 00:52:43,000
I'll go without soup for a month.
I think I can handle it.

707
00:52:43,000 --> 00:52:44,667
Will that be enough?

708
00:52:44,667 --> 00:52:46,700
Not enough?

709
00:52:46,700 --> 00:52:48,633
I'm really sorry.

710
00:52:49,333 --> 00:52:51,200
What exactly are you sorry for?

711
00:52:52,533 --> 00:52:56,433
I mean, I really was going to come home,
even if it was late, but...

712
00:52:56,433 --> 00:52:58,367
Oh, is that all you have to say?

713
00:53:01,900 --> 00:53:03,833
I was going to come home
no matter how late it was.

714
00:53:03,833 --> 00:53:07,067
I even booked the last train ticket.

715
00:53:07,067 --> 00:53:09,400
How could you do this to me?

716
00:53:09,400 --> 00:53:10,600
That's how reporting is, you know.

717
00:53:10,600 --> 00:53:11,680
Once a story breaks,

718
00:53:11,680 --> 00:53:14,800
one thing leads to another,
and it just keeps snowballing...

719
00:53:14,800 --> 00:53:17,133
How could you only buy something for Yul?

720
00:53:17,133 --> 00:53:18,733
What?

721
00:53:21,600 --> 00:53:26,867
Yul, you can only have two. No more, okay?

722
00:53:28,533 --> 00:53:32,300
How could you only buy
the cream-flavored walnut cakes?

723
00:53:33,967 --> 00:53:36,633
You like red bean filling, right?

724
00:53:36,633 --> 00:53:38,133
I really do.

725
00:53:38,133 --> 00:53:40,700
Ever since we first met
about seven years ago,

726
00:53:40,700 --> 00:53:44,800
I think I've only eaten red bean bread,
red bean porridge, and red bean noodles...

727
00:53:44,800 --> 00:53:47,333
Did you already forget that?

728
00:53:47,333 --> 00:53:48,867
I remember.

729
00:53:48,867 --> 00:53:51,167
But how could you...

730
00:53:51,167 --> 00:53:56,000
Yul, put that down.
No, you can't have more than two.

731
00:53:56,000 --> 00:53:57,200
Eat it after dinner.

732
00:53:57,200 --> 00:53:58,867
Okay.

733
00:53:59,733 --> 00:54:02,600
But how could you...

734
00:54:02,600 --> 00:54:05,933
This is the mouth that has no excuses.

735
00:54:06,700 --> 00:54:08,467
- You laughed!
- No, I didn't.

736
00:54:08,467 --> 00:54:09,933
Huh? You laughed.

737
00:54:09,933 --> 00:54:11,667
You laughed! It's over when you smile.

738
00:54:11,667 --> 00:54:13,933
Yul, Mommy laughed!

739
00:54:16,033 --> 00:54:18,333
I'm letting it slide because of Yul, okay?

740
00:54:18,333 --> 00:54:21,167
I'm letting it go because Yul
helped make things easier for me.

741
00:54:21,167 --> 00:54:22,900
Yeah.

742
00:54:28,633 --> 00:54:32,367
Yul did that? Did you help Mommy
even for Daddy's sake?

743
00:54:32,367 --> 00:54:35,067
Oh, my, so cute!

744
00:54:35,067 --> 00:54:37,967
No, wash your hands before touching her.
Yul already took a bath.

745
00:54:37,967 --> 00:54:40,200
I won't touch her. I'll just hug her.

746
00:54:40,200 --> 00:54:42,767
You're my precious treasure.

747
00:54:42,767 --> 00:54:44,933
Right, how was your first day back at work?

748
00:54:44,933 --> 00:54:45,933
After such a long time...

749
00:54:45,933 --> 00:54:47,867
Yul, let's eat after dinner.

750
00:54:47,867 --> 00:54:50,333
- You'll get scolded by Mommy.
- Well, everyone helped me out.

751
00:54:50,333 --> 00:54:53,233
Still, it's something I've done for
a long time, so it came back quickly.

752
00:54:53,233 --> 00:54:55,900
I knew you'd do great. I told you, right?

753
00:54:55,900 --> 00:54:58,100
You'd get back into
the swing of things quickly.

754
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:03,467
Honey, go wash up quickly. We need to eat.

755
00:55:03,467 --> 00:55:06,433
No, you're tired.
Let's just make do with this today.

756
00:55:06,433 --> 00:55:09,567
Sure, if you say so.
But it's still samgyetang.

757
00:55:09,567 --> 00:55:11,467
Samgyetang?

758
00:55:12,667 --> 00:55:14,333
Yul, she says it's samgyetang.

759
00:55:14,333 --> 00:55:16,567
I will go wash up quickly, okay?

760
00:55:24,567 --> 00:55:26,467
The tenant from Tae Seong Chicken
on the first floor

761
00:55:26,467 --> 00:55:30,767
wanted to visit and greet you in person,
but I declined on your behalf.

762
00:55:30,767 --> 00:55:35,267
But they want to send you a gift.
What should I do?

763
00:55:40,833 --> 00:55:42,567
Honey, can you get me a towel?

764
00:55:42,567 --> 00:55:44,533
Yeah, hold on!

765
00:55:45,833 --> 00:55:47,600
Please politely decline.

766
00:55:47,600 --> 00:55:50,600
And I'll also freeze the rent for next month.

767
00:55:50,600 --> 00:55:52,633
- Thank you for the meal!
- Eat plenty.

768
00:55:52,633 --> 00:55:54,400
Yul, try this.

769
00:55:55,400 --> 00:55:56,733
- Is it good?
- Yeah.

770
00:55:56,733 --> 00:55:58,144
It's super, super good!

771
00:55:58,144 --> 00:56:00,300
Super, super good?

772
00:56:00,300 --> 00:56:02,567
But Yul, didn't you miss Daddy?

773
00:56:02,567 --> 00:56:04,133
- I missed you!
- How much?

774
00:56:04,133 --> 00:56:05,567
This much!

775
00:56:05,567 --> 00:56:07,800
You missed him this much?

776
00:56:07,800 --> 00:56:10,300
Dance as much as you enjoy the food!

777
00:56:27,840 --> 00:56:32,384
[Ok's Flower Shop]

778
00:56:39,100 --> 00:56:42,133
You're early! Did you change your schedule?

779
00:56:42,133 --> 00:56:44,300
Well, right. You have to go to work now.

780
00:56:44,300 --> 00:56:47,400
Why did you open so early?
The sun isn't even up yet.

781
00:56:47,400 --> 00:56:51,767
I need to catch customers on their way
to work. Making a living is tough.

782
00:56:51,767 --> 00:56:55,567
I thought you'd finally have some free time
after sending your kid to daycare.

783
00:56:55,567 --> 00:56:57,700
How does it feel to be back?

784
00:56:58,867 --> 00:57:00,333
My life is about to get a lot busier.

785
00:57:00,333 --> 00:57:03,400
And the world will get noisier, huh?

786
00:57:06,267 --> 00:57:07,933
What flower is this? Is it cosmos?

787
00:57:07,933 --> 00:57:08,933
It's a marguerite.

788
00:57:08,933 --> 00:57:09,967
Oh, marguerite.

789
00:57:09,967 --> 00:57:13,700
Its flower meanings are
"revealing secrets" and "true love."

790
00:57:13,700 --> 00:57:17,467
Come to think of it, this one flower
contains both "secret" and "truth."

791
00:57:17,467 --> 00:57:19,833
"A truthful person has no secrets."

792
00:57:19,833 --> 00:57:22,933
"True love means revealing your secrets."
Is that what it means?

793
00:57:22,933 --> 00:57:25,800
Well, I don't really like that meaning.

794
00:57:25,800 --> 00:57:28,900
Sometimes you keep secrets
because you love someone too much.

795
00:57:31,700 --> 00:57:34,300
Aren't you worried that

796
00:57:34,300 --> 00:57:37,633
the day might come
when your husband finds out?

797
00:57:42,800 --> 00:57:45,533
Well, the night before I went back to work,

798
00:57:45,533 --> 00:57:47,853
my husband promised he'd come home early,

799
00:57:47,853 --> 00:57:50,333
but then he suddenly had to go out of town.

800
00:57:50,333 --> 00:57:53,400
He said he'd come home
even if it was late, but he never did.

801
00:57:53,400 --> 00:57:54,433
Oh, dear.

802
00:57:54,433 --> 00:57:57,767
I knew it was because of his reporting,
but I was still hurt.

803
00:57:57,767 --> 00:58:00,967
I was busy getting ready,
but I just got upset for no reason.

804
00:58:00,967 --> 00:58:04,064
"Kwon Tae Seong, just you wait
till you get home tonight."

805
00:58:04,064 --> 00:58:08,667
There I was, all fired up by myself,
and then I just ended up laughing.

806
00:58:09,500 --> 00:58:12,333
I found myself so strange and amazing.

807
00:58:12,333 --> 00:58:15,333
And I still can't believe moments like that.

808
00:58:16,500 --> 00:58:18,133
I love them.

809
00:58:20,400 --> 00:58:22,633
So I'm not worried.

810
00:58:23,367 --> 00:58:25,700
Because that day will never come.

811
00:58:38,267 --> 00:58:41,433
He's someone who lives in the light.

812
00:58:41,433 --> 00:58:44,300
Because he's different from me.

813
00:58:44,300 --> 00:58:47,833
Because if he knew how different we are,
we couldn't stay together.

814
00:58:47,833 --> 00:58:50,633
You don't really know much about me, do you?

815
00:58:50,633 --> 00:58:52,700
I don't know much about you, Bo Na.

816
00:58:53,833 --> 00:58:55,967
I know your name, but...

817
00:58:57,067 --> 00:58:59,233
I don't even know if it's your real name.

818
00:59:00,833 --> 00:59:04,000
Where you were born, how you grew up...

819
00:59:16,400 --> 00:59:21,167
What your family is like,
or what you do for a living...

820
00:59:26,467 --> 00:59:27,872
Why you were standing there

821
00:59:27,872 --> 00:59:30,767
- on the day we first met?
- Hold on!

822
00:59:30,767 --> 00:59:33,167
- Come down, now!
- I don't know those things either.

823
00:59:33,167 --> 00:59:34,800
Oh, slowly!

824
00:59:34,800 --> 00:59:38,767
But I do know some aspects of you, Bo Na.

825
00:59:38,767 --> 00:59:41,067
Perhaps love begins...

826
00:59:42,067 --> 00:59:44,167
when you find yourself drawn to

827
00:59:44,167 --> 00:59:47,667
just one side of a person
among all the many sides they have.

828
00:59:50,633 --> 00:59:53,133
I've already fallen in love.

829
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:02,867
My name is Yoo Bo Na. It's my real name.

830
01:00:04,967 --> 01:00:09,400
Please take care of me.
It's my first time with love.

831
01:00:11,833 --> 01:00:15,433
I'm not worried.
Because that day will never come.

832
01:00:15,433 --> 01:00:20,667
Because the day he sees
my other side will never come.

833
01:00:24,000 --> 01:00:25,000
Breaking news.

834
01:00:25,000 --> 01:00:30,133
A shooting using a sniper rifle
has occurred in the heart of Seoul.

835
01:00:30,133 --> 01:00:34,667
Some speculate that Kingfisher,
the infamous serial gun killer

836
01:00:34,667 --> 01:00:37,167
[Breaking News: Kingfisher Returns?]
who disappeared for the past four years,

837
01:00:37,167 --> 01:00:39,467
[Shooting Homicide in Seoul]
may have returned.

838
01:00:39,467 --> 01:00:42,933
The incident took place at a hotel
in Jeonjak-dong, Seoul.

839
01:00:42,933 --> 01:00:44,933
A man in his thirties,
identified as Mr. Hwang,

840
01:00:44,933 --> 01:00:49,533
was struck and killed by a bullet
fired from outside the building.

841
01:00:49,533 --> 01:00:52,867
For more details, we'll soon connect live to
our reporter on the scene

842
01:00:52,867 --> 01:00:55,233
for the latest on the police investigation...

843
01:01:48,967 --> 01:01:50,800
A gun murder in South Korea?

844
01:01:50,800 --> 01:01:52,400
I think that punk is back.

845
01:01:52,400 --> 01:01:54,467
From now on, you're going
after Kingfisher, right?

846
01:01:54,467 --> 01:01:55,833
I'll really give it my all this time.

847
01:01:55,833 --> 01:01:56,833
Is it really the Kingfisher?

848
01:01:56,833 --> 01:01:58,432
[Musan Drug Kingpin's Car Explosion]
You're covering the Kingfisher story, right?

849
01:01:58,432 --> 01:01:59,967
Like, you find anything at the shooting site.

850
01:01:59,967 --> 01:02:01,033
Did you come here knowing something?

851
01:02:01,033 --> 01:02:03,433
Hey, you never know.
What if that was the real clue?

852
01:02:03,433 --> 01:02:04,480
[I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]
But sometimes,

853
01:02:04,480 --> 01:02:06,767
[Security Alert]
I think that day might actually come.

854
01:02:06,767 --> 01:02:08,767
He might find me.

855
01:02:08,767 --> 01:02:09,933
Shall I schedule a meeting?

856
01:02:09,933 --> 01:02:11,133
Don't you think something's strange?

857
01:02:11,133 --> 01:02:12,672
[Yoo Bo Na, Husband, Company]
Honestly, a guy like him

858
01:02:12,672 --> 01:02:14,432
getting gunned down
by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

859
01:02:14,432 --> 01:02:18,633
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

860
01:02:21,200 --> 01:02:23,233
Where's Kwon Tae Seong?
